  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084349",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-140504",
      "knowledge_point_id": "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Symmetric Matrices",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\"",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$P,$ $Q,$ and $R$",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$Q$ and $R$ only",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$P$ and $Q$ only",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "None of the matrices are symmetric",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$P$ and $R$ only",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "6086ee72196fa1c006e2591f3a7691e522f58789aaed22133a3dbfa05dfaa317"
      },
      "difficulty": "easy",
