  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-72492",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$C$ only",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$A$ only",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$B$ and $C$ only",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
