  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084856",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-90524",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ba3e0748-2a14-547e-b21e-c34251994a94",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Differential Equation Satisfied by the Reduction of Order Function",
      "problem": "The function ${y}_{1}(t)={t}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation ${t}^{2}{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}+3y=0$ for $t>0.$ If ${y}_{2}=u(t){y}_{1}(t)$ is a second solution of the equation, then which of the following equations must be satisfied by $u(t)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=u(t){y}_{1}(t)=u{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{t}^{3}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{t}^{3}+3u{t}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{t}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+6ut.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}({u}^{″}{t}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+6ut)-3t({u}^{′}{t}^{3}+3u{t}^{2})+3u{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3}({u}^{″}{t}^{2}+6{u}^{′}t+6u-3{u}^{′}t-9u+3u) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3}({u}^{″}{t}^{2}+3{u}^{′}t) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{4}({u}^{″}t+3{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${t}^{4}\\ne 0$ for $t>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\nt{u}^{″}+3{u}^{′}=0.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{u}^{″}+2{t}^{3}u=0",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3{u}^{″}-{t}^{3}u=0",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{t}^{3}{u}^{″}-{u}^{′}=0",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "t{u}^{″}+3{u}^{′}=0",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4{u}^{″}+t{u}^{′}=0",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
